 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "56: the oath is framed («كذبًا وباطلا»). 57: a mountain for «مغارات» (no people, no cave opening). 58 frames the criticism («ليس… لقصد صحيح»). 59:11-15 supplies the unspoken answer with As-Sa'di's «لسلموا من النفاق ولهدوا إلى الإيمان…». Coins for «الصدقات», geometric for «حسبنا الله», light for «سيؤتينا الله من فضله». 59: short-word flag, listen. STAGING v4: c1 (56-57): a town by day. Three men (the hypocrites) walk in from the right and swear toward three believers standing on the left (Al-Muyassar: they swear to you, believers); they speak on 56:1 and 56:4; the believers do nothing. 57 is a counterfactual (if they found a refuge they would rush to it): nobody flees; only the mountain plate (57:5, caves) and the camera on them. c2 (58-59) stays ambient under a night sky (no central light source), with the background quiet over 58:1-5 (Allah addresses the Prophet about those who find fault with him): 58 is their criticism of the Prophet's own distribution of the alms (no giver may stand in for him and nobody may speak toward an empty side) and 59 is a counterfactual full of the Name. The plates of 59 are now one geometric plate from 59:9 to the end (the light plate that drew one word before the Name on 59:11 is removed). The cover now shows them swearing to the believers (56:4)."
 },
